# cargo's build directory -- `just dsrs serve` builds `target/release/quizd.exe` here. The corpus,
# templates and assets are embedded, so that one file IS the deployment and has no business in the
# repo. Cargo.lock IS checked in: this crate builds a binary, so the exact dependency versions the
# numbers in RESULTS.md were measured against are part of the record.
/target/

# flamegraphs and profile output, if anything is ever pointed at this
/*.svg
/perf.data*

# The repo root ignores `*.html`, because at the root every .html is a BML build artifact. These are
# not -- they are the askama source templates, compiled into the binary at build time.
!/templates/*.html
